(6990705, 1054830, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pamb:</b></div><hr/><i> Goodness. I seriously thought this would finish much much higher. You were ripped. :(<br/>Terrific shot, love the movement, the colour and the fact that you got the dice sharp too. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks pamb - perhaps people thought it was smoke and not motion blur or perhaps the competition was just too good. There was no smoke involved of course - just a couple of dice in my kitchen on some black card with a small torch as a light source and a second curtain flash (I think that is what it was called - it was first time I had used this so the challenge was excellent for teaching me a new trick)<br/> <br/>I had wanted to do this with white dice but the only dice I could find in the house were red semi-transparent dice so had to make do.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-03-04 02:36:15.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by pamb: Goodness. I seriously thought this would finish much much higher. You were ripped. :(Terrific shot, love the movement, the colour and the fact that you got the dice sharp too.   Thanks pamb - perhaps people thought it was smoke and not motion blur or perhaps the competition was just too good. There was no smoke involved of course - just a couple of dice in my kitchen on some black card with a small torch as a light source and a second curtain flash (I think that is what it was called - it was first time I had used this so the challenge was excellent for teaching me a new trick) I had wanted to do this with white dice but the only dice I could find in the house were red semi-transparent dice so had to make do.', '2013-03-04 02:34:52.000000', '2013-03-04 02:36:15.000000', 0),
